  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"60\" data-end=\"278\">The <strong data-start=\"64\" data-end=\"80\">Tzanck smear</strong> is a rapid, cytological test performed on the <strong data-start=\"127\" data-end=\"157\">fluid or base of a vesicle</strong>, typically to aid in the diagnosis of <strong data-start=\"196\" data-end=\"228\">viral infections of the skin</strong>, particularly <strong data-start=\"243\" data-end=\"266\">herpesvirus-related</strong> conditions.</p>\n<p data-start=\"60\" data-end=\"278\">This test is used to detect&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"323\" data-end=\"353\">multinucleated giant cells</strong> or other cytopathic effects caused by <strong data-start=\"392\" data-end=\"422\">Herpes Simplex Virus (HSV)</strong>, <strong data-start=\"424\" data-end=\"456\">Varicella Zoster Virus (VZV)</strong>, or related infections.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Finding</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Multinucleated giant cells</strong></td>\n<td>Suggestive of <strong>Herpes Simplex Virus (HSV)</strong> or <strong>Varicella Zoster Virus (VZV)</strong> infection.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Acantholytic cells (Tzanck cells)</strong></td>\n<td>Detached keratinocytes with large nuclei &ndash; seen in <strong>HSV, VZV</strong>, and <strong>pemphigus vulgaris</strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>No giant cells or acantholysis</strong></td>\n<td>Test is likely <strong>negative</strong> for herpesvirus or pemphigus &ndash; consider alternative diagnoses.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1437\" data-end=\"1494\"><strong data-start=\"1441\" data-end=\"1494\">Clinical Conditions Where Tzanck Smear Is Helpful</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1495\" data-end=\"1679\">\n<li data-start=\"1495\" data-end=\"1532\">\n<p data-start=\"1497\" data-end=\"1532\"><strong data-start=\"1497\" data-end=\"1515\">Herpes Simplex</strong> (HSV-1 or HSV-2)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1533\" data-end=\"1579\">\n<p data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1579\"><strong data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1563\">Herpes Zoster (Shingles)</strong> &ndash; caused by VZV</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1580\" data-end=\"1608\">\n<p data-start=\"1582\" data-end=\"1608\"><strong data-start=\"1582\" data-end=\"1608\">Varicella (Chickenpox)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1609\" data-end=\"1679\">\n<p data-start=\"1611\" data-end=\"1679\"><strong data-start=\"1611\" data-end=\"1633\">Pemphigus vulgaris</strong> &ndash; shows acantholysis without viral inclusions</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"1686\" data-end=\"1705\"><strong data-start=\"1690\" data-end=\"1705\">Limitations</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1706\" data-end=\"1944\">\n<li data-start=\"1706\" data-end=\"1825\">\n<p data-start=\"1708\" data-end=\"1825\"><strong data-start=\"1708\" data-end=\"1732\">Cannot differentiate</strong> between HSV-1, HSV-2, and VZV &ndash; further testing (PCR or viral culture) is needed for typing.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1826\" data-end=\"1892\">\n<p data-start=\"1828\" data-end=\"1892\"><strong data-start=\"1828\" data-end=\"1862\">Not very sensitive or specific</strong> &ndash; false negatives are common.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1893\" data-end=\"1944\">\n<p data-start=\"1895\" data-end=\"1944\"><strong data-start=\"1895\" data-end=\"1944\">Does not detect bacteria or fungal pathogens.</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
